course: dictionary
lesson: 6371
title: Muddle and muddled
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: The word muddle can be a noun, a verb or an adjective. A muddle is an untidy mess or a state of confusion: «My drawer is in a muddle.» Here the drawer is not neat, so muddle means a messy heap of things.
explain: To muddle things means to mix them up or put them in the wrong order. «Apostrophes cause the worst muddles.» The apostrophes are not in the right places, so the writing gets mixed up. Check the words around the word: they tell you what is mixed up.
explain: If you feel confused and cannot think clearly, you are muddled, or you are in a muddle. In maths, pupils can get muddled with the steps. «Olympiad puzzles hand you a chain in a muddle.» The steps are out of order, so you must find the first step and then follow each «so...» to the end.
explain: In the UK, to muddle through means to manage somehow, even without a good plan. You may not know the perfect method, but you still get the job done.
fact: Muddle can be a noun (a muddle), a verb (to muddle) or an adjective (muddled).
fact: «Muddle» means an untidy mess, or things mixed up in the wrong order.
fact: «Muddled» means confused, or unable to think clearly.
fact: «Muddle up» means to mix up. «Muddle through» means to manage somehow, without a good plan.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «My drawer is in a muddle.» What does in a muddle mean? | Very cold | *An untidy mess | A tidy row of books | A place to keep shoes
exercise: Mia says, «I got muddled on the maths steps.» What does muddled mean here? | *Confused and unable to think clearly | Very quick and clever | Happy and proud | Finished early
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means mixed up: «Apostrophes cause the worst muddles.» | *muddles | cause | worst | apostrophes
test: «Please do not muddle the two cups.» What does muddle mean here? | *To mix them up or put them in the wrong order | To hide them under the table | To wash them carefully | To count them slowly
test: Which phrase means to manage somehow, without a good plan? | Clean away | *Muddle through | Tidy up | Put in order
exam: «Olympiad puzzles hand you a chain in a muddle.» What does a chain in a muddle mean? | A long list of happy stories | A chain that is very short | *A set of steps that are mixed up and out of order | A clean, shiny chain for a bike
